  {
    "day": 4,
    "theme": "Clusters",
    "date": "2026-11-04",
    "title": "Every US power plant",
    "blurb": "Every operating US power plant in EIA Form 860M (September 2026), clustered on the map, with each ring showing the cluster's nameplate capacity by fuel. Gas is 41% of the 1,417 GW, while solar is 12% even though half of all plants are solar. Texas has the most battery storage, 19.4 GW to California's 16.5 GW.",
    "alt": "Dark map of the lower 48 covered in donut-shaped clusters, each labeled with its total capacity, from 296 MW in northern Maine to 221 GW around Indiana and Ohio. Ring segments show the fuel mix: mostly coral gas across Texas and the Southeast, blue hydro in the Pacific Northwest, green wind on the Plains, and yellow solar with purple batteries in Southern California.",
